      "choice_rule": "Four real Grade 2 contractions with apostrophes. Exactly one is the short form of the two target words in the stem. The other three are different real contractions. Prefer same-pronoun pairs (I'm/I've/I'll) or nearby n't forms (don't/doesn't/didn't; won't/wouldn't/weren't). Never offer two-word expanded forms. Never drop the apostrophe (dont, isnt, theyre). When the stem has is not, are not, or will not, the answer is isn't, aren't, or won't, not 's not or 're not.",
