  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Choices are four real contractions with apostrophes. Never change the skill into expanded two-word answers.",
      "Exactly one choice shortens the two target words in the stem. The other three must be real contractions that do not match those words.",
      "Never use wordlist typos that drop the apostrophe, such as dont, isnt, theyre, youre, wont, or im.",
      "Tier 1 distractors stay on the same pronoun: I'm with I've, I'll, or I'd; she's with he's, I'm, or we're.",
      "Tier 2 and 3 distractors are nearby n't or will/have forms: don't/doesn't/didn't; isn't/aren't/wasn't; we'll/we've/we're; won't/wouldn't/weren't.",
      "Do not write stems where two classroom contractions both fit, such as he is not (he's vs isn't).",
      "Keep stems in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands and no real names."
    ]
  },
